  "term": "stepfamily",
  "definition": "A stepfamily is a newly formed family structure that may develop after changes such as parents’ separation. In this context, becoming a stepfamily is described as a period of instability for young people that can require substantial coping and adjustment, especially when other stressors are also present.",
